  "source_review": [
    "Authenticated complete original16.2.14 a11y declarations and both advertised21.2.14/22.1.7 minimum public entries resolve FocusableOption, ListKeyManagerOption and FocusOrigin to unchanged declaration bodies. The option interface inherits optional disabled:boolean and getLabel():string, and requires focus(origin?:FocusOrigin):void. Public declarations and members have no deprecated/private/removal/experimental tags.",
    "Six exact authored imports are used only in erased implements clauses on MatLegacyChip, MatLegacyListOption, MatLegacyButton, _MatTabLinkBase, _MatCheckboxBase and _MatOptionBase. The seventh is an erased intersection type for paginated tab-header items. Resolved TypeScript import symbols exclude shadows, extra import routes and runtime value/extends use.",
    "Each actual complete source file emits identical executable JavaScript when the option-interface import is removed, using the real library target/module/decorator/import-helper options and no decorator metadata. This proves import erasure; it does not claim Angular AOT or the complete owned class compiles.",
    "Strict isolated copies of the exact complete three-interface/alias declaration closure prove six structural equalities and twelve assignment directions between tag and minimums. Eighteen valid optional focus argument cases and twenty-one type-negative controls preserve required focus, optional state/label and the accepted origin domain. No declaration body is replaced by a candidate expectation.",
    "Twelve counterexamples reject value use, missing/duplicate/private imports, runtime inheritance and changed focus, disabled, label or origin contracts. No component TypeScript, resources, selectors, behavior, token identity, package floors or consumer code changed. Focus routing, monitor/key-manager behavior and lifecycle remain separate obligations."
  ],
